course: dictionary
lesson: 3236
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word envelope has two main meanings. The first is a flat paper cover for a letter or card. The second is any covering that wraps something, like the layer of gases around a planet.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «He writes on the back of an envelope: food £45, bus fares £20, power £15.» He is not posting a letter here. He is doing quick rough sums on a piece of paper, so the envelope is the paper he writes on.
explain: Context can also show you what a thing is for. «At New Year Lín's aunties hand out hóngbāo — red envelopes with money inside — and every child in the room suddenly remembers their manners.» The story tells you that a red envelope is a gift of money that children are happy to receive.
explain: Some phrases use envelope in a different way. «Seal an envelope» and «address an envelope» are about paper and post. But «push the envelope» means trying new, bolder things. When the context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: An envelope is a flat paper cover for a letter or card.
fact: «Envelope» can also mean any covering that wraps something, like the gases around a planet.
fact: «Hóngbāo» means a red envelope with money inside, given as a gift.
fact: «Address an envelope» means writing the name, street, town and postcode on it.
fact: «Push the envelope» means trying new, bolder things.
exercise: «He writes on the back of an envelope: food £45, bus fares £20, power £15.» What is the envelope used for here? | *A piece of paper for quick rough sums | A bag for shopping | A flat paper cover for a letter | A stamp
exercise: At New Year Lín's aunties hand out «hóngbāo». What does hóngbāo mean? | A shop opening | *A red envelope with money inside | A lion dance costume | A joke rhyme
exercise: A planet is wrapped in layers of gases. What might envelope mean in this sentence? | A bag of sweets | A card with a picture on it | A letter sent by post | *Any covering that wraps something
test: «Please address the envelope before you post the card.» What does address mean here? | *Write the name, street and town on it | Find the way home | Lick the stamp | Speak to a crowd in a loud voice
test: The phrase «push the envelope» means what? | Make a paper cover thinner | Lose your way | Post a letter very fast | *Try new, bolder things
exam: «"bié dāngmiàn chāi" means "don't open it in front of them", a parent's whispered reminder about presents and red envelopes.» What is the parent reminding the child? | *Not to open the present or red envelope in front of the giver | To hang the red envelopes up by the lion dance | To open all the envelopes as soon as possible | To post the red envelopes to the shop
